    "etymology": {
     "text": "Pictogram of a person with both hands at the waist; the original meaning was ‘waist’, now written 腰.",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "The character once meant ‘waist’ — when it was borrowed for ‘want’, the flesh radical was added to make a new character 腰."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
